  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In order to consider the REST API stable (non-beta), we need to finish several pieces of it and make sure certain bugs are addressed.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "After this point, we will not make backward-incompatible changes without giving sufficient warning to users.  Ideally, this means marking functionality as deprecated for a release, so people have time to adjust their client code.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In the committer discussion on Nov 10 '09, we agreed that stabilizing the REST API does ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "not",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " require that the relationship-related methods are exposed in it.  A future version of Fedora may extend the REST API to add these.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
