  "description": "<p>In order to consider the REST API stable (non-beta), we need to finish several pieces of it and make sure certain bugs are addressed.</p>\n\n<p>After this point, we will not make backward-incompatible changes without giving sufficient warning to users.  Ideally, this means marking functionality as deprecated for a release, so people have time to adjust their client code.</p>\n\n<p>In the committer discussion on Nov 10 '09, we agreed that stabilizing the REST API does <b>not</b> require that the relationship-related methods are exposed in it.  A future version of Fedora may extend the REST API to add these.</p>",
